# Jira board hygiene

This repo is tracked in Jira project `PT`. Use the sibling `jira-cli` (`python jira.py` from that repo). Do not leave tickets sitting in To Do after work has started, and do not mark them Done unless the acceptance criteria are actually met in code.

## Status

- Move a story to **In Progress** when you start it. Name the branch after the key when practical (`feature/pt-23-…`).
- Move it to **Done** only after the criteria are implemented and verified (tests, or the closest substitute).
- Close a parent epic only when every child story is Done. If one child is still open, the epic stays In Progress.
- Create tickets when new work appears (quality-loop stories, follow-ups, bugs). Do not silently expand an existing story past its description.

## Comments

Add a comment when something would otherwise live only in the agent's head:

- A decision (why Zod `.strict()`, why validation is in the step not the client)
- A discovery (the TypeScript type was compile-time only; a criterion was already satisfied)
- A gap (what was *not* done, and why the ticket stayed open)

Write comments in Jira wiki markup via `python jira.py comment KEY --body-file <file-or-->`. Do not put secrets, tokens, or local machine paths in comments.
